.TH WMT-PLAY 1
.SH NAME
wmt-play \- WonderMedia WM8505 MJPEG video player
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmt-play
.RB [ \-s
.IR sec ]
.RB [ \-l ]
.RB [ \-a ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.I file
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wmt-play
is a fullscreen video player for the WonderMedia WM8505, playing MJPEG AVI
files.
The video hardware decodes each frame and scales it to the panel, keeping
its aspect ratio.
Only 16-bit PCM audio is played.
.PP
It runs under X, which leases it the display for the length of playback.
Audio plays through the ALSA
.B front
device of the default sound card, and
.B wmt-play
holds the card until it exits.
If another program is using the sound card,
.B wmt-play
exits with an error.
The
.B \-a
option plays the video silently.
.PP
Files are prepared on another computer with
.BR ffmpeg (1),
using the
.B \%wmt-encode.sh
script from the wmt-play source.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-s " sec"
Start
.I sec
seconds into the file.
.TP
.B \-l
Loop the file.
.TP
.B \-a
Disable audio.
.TP
.B \-v
Print the presentation time, clock, and dropped frame count at each frame.
.TP
.B \-h
Print usage and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Space
Pause or resume.
.TP
.BR Left ", " Right
Seek back or forward 5 seconds.
.TP
.BR Down ", " Up
Seek back or forward 30 seconds.
.TP
.BR Comma ", " Period
Step back or forward one frame while paused.
.TP
.BR q ", " Escape
Quit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR wmt (4)
